  "cover_text": "Georgetown — Sally Long, a long-time resident of the Kauaʻi Natural Farms Preserve near Georgetown, recently founded a new habitat for endangered native birds.\nEnvironmental Conservation Manager Kelly Driver tells McLean's Demetric Jola and David Klukak that Long leaped out of airplane vacavels and won a search...Stay tuned for more ever updates on this project.Beneficial tree has come up, cutting back unwanted grass and weeds. It’s not your best example but it is in a great spot that is especially important to the native birds that use this preserve’s forest for foraging, spacing-up and nesting sites.\nThis preserve also features a cutting off to protect a long-horn cow family from mature invasive alien foxes.\nThis site",
